1. History: Initial state instance 0 checkpoint 0. Write data unit D0 for key k with jsn (0,1) but crash before journal records are written. Units are written but not published. Recovery starts instance 1. Scans journal finds no records. Instance 1 crashes before writing instance watermark row for instance 0. Recovery starts instance 2. Scans journal finds no records. Writes instance watermark row for instance 1 with value 0. No row exists for instance 0. For root R (instance 2 checkpoint 0) the rule computes current version of k as D0. Truth: D0 was not published (no journal records) so k has no current version.

2. History: Initial state instance 0 checkpoint 0. Write data unit D0 for key k with jsn (0,1) but crash before journal records are written. Units are written but not published. Recovery starts instance 1. Scans journal finds no records. Instance 1 crashes before writing instance watermark row for instance 0. Recovery starts instance 2. Scans journal finds no records. Writes instance watermark row for instance 1 with value 0. No row exists for instance 0. For root R (instance 2 checkpoint 0) the rule computes current version of k as D0. Truth: D0 was not published (no journal records) so k has no current version.

3. Reserving jsn before writing units does not break journal rules. A transaction reserves jsn (i,c) writes units crashes before journal records. Recovery stops at gap (i,c) as expected. Journal rules are satisfied.

4. Scrub watermark can be wrong after crash during scrub. Scrub starts invalidates garbage units up to checkpoint 5 then crashes. Scrub watermark not updated. Next scrub starts from beginning. No resurrection window because freed space reallocation is blocked by checkpoint publication rule. Tombstone reclamation depends on scrub watermark but scrub watermark being wrong does not cause wrong current version.

5. Container rebirth does not break anything. Clone head C rewrites container takes new identity birth tree C. Snapshot S taken before rebirth. For root S the rewritten container has birth checkpoint higher than S's checkpoint so not visible. Origin head O rewrites container after clone checkpoint so not visible to C. Second clone C2 of O rewrites container takes new identity. Correct visibility.

6. Proposal does not contradict background facts. Freed space reallocation is blocked by checkpoint publication rule. Freeing space does not require allocation as scrub invalidates headers in place. Journal rules are respected with jsn reservation. Instance watermark rows are exempt from K generation deletion as specified.
